.TH QYPR-BAR 1 "2026-07-17" "qypr-bar" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qypr-bar \- lean GPU-free Wayland desktop status bar (waybar replacement)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qypr-bar
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qypr-bar
is a memory-efficient, GPU-free status bar for the unlocked desktop. It hosts
the same status bar as
.BR qypr-lock (1)
\(em the same indicators, Quick Settings panel, and popovers \(em but on a
.B wlr-layer-shell-unstable-v1
surface instead of a session-lock surface, so it runs as a normal desktop
panel on any Wayland compositor that implements layer-shell (Hyprland, Sway,
river, ...). It is software-rendered with cairo and
.BR wl_shm .
.PP
The bar anchors a full-width, chromeless strip to the top of each output and
reserves an exclusive zone, so tiled windows never sit underneath it. A subtle
backdrop keeps the glyphs legible over any wallpaper. When Quick Settings or a
detail popover opens, the surface grows to the full output height so the
overlay is visible and takes input, then shrinks back so the desktop keeps its
clicks.
.PP
Unlike the lock screen, the bar reveals the session-sensitive widgets that are
always hidden while locked:
.TP
.B Workspaces
a pill per workspace via the standard
.B ext-workspace-v1
protocol; the active one is accented, urgent ones tinted, and a click switches
workspace. Hidden/special workspaces are filtered.
.TP
.B Active window
the focused window's title (application id fallback) via
.BR wlr-foreign-toplevel-management ,
following keyboard focus.
.PP
No compositor-specific IPC is used (no
.BR hyprctl );
every backend speaks a standard Wayland protocol or freedesktop/systemd
interface, so the bar is portable across compositors.
.SH INDICATORS
Clock, battery (UPower), WiFi (NetworkManager), Bluetooth (BlueZ), volume
(PipeWire via libpulse), brightness (logind/sysfs), Do Not Disturb, and a
StatusNotifierItem tray host for third-party icons \(em plus the workspaces and
active-window widgets above. Left-click activates an indicator or opens its
detail; scrolling over the volume/brightness indicators adjusts them; the gear
opens Quick Settings.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
The compositor socket to connect to.
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Required by Wayland for socket exchange.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal shutdown.
.TP
.B 1
The compositor is unreachable or does not implement
.BR wlr-layer-shell-unstable-v1 .
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Run the bar (typically from the compositor's autostart):
.B qypr-bar &
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qypr-lock (1),
.BR qypr-record (1),
.BR waybar (1),
.BR hyprctl (1)
.SH AUTHORS
The qypr project.
